Z||000005||Haze||06-27-2001||12:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87 Pegasus:<BR><B>Does any one that is with N.I.F.E. know of any shows besides the ones we have in our newsletter that are taking place this year...such as Gary Lang in McHenry, Frankfort Car show in Frankfort, IL...  or any other please let me know...  thank you<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey 87 Pegasus,<BR>  I think I'm going to "FIEROS IN FRANKENMUTH" July 13th, 14th & 15th. (Only if Hazette is feeling better by then)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cooltext2087.jpg">  </A>||||reg||10
Z||000006||Oreif||06-27-2001||02:13 AM||||Aside from the NIFE newsletter, Paul V's website, and here I also scan thru the below links. )<BR> <A HREF="http://www.hotrodsworldwide.com/shows.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.hotrodsworldwide.com/shows.htm</A> <BR>Most are many different types of cars and usually Fiero's a few. But it is always fun to attend. The Shellbyville, IL is usually a good one to go to. I went there a few years ago and it was a blast. It's in the middle of July. It's about 2.5- 3.0 hours south of here. (See July 20th) This site also lists show all over the U.S., Canada, and even Sweden!<P> <A HREF="http://www.poci.org" TARGET=_blank>http://www.poci.org</A> <BR>Listing of the Pontiac Oakland Club events.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Archie||06-27-2001||07:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ferrari_momo:<BR><B>hey, if u run to Gary Smith, please tell him i say hi.  he is a fiero buddy of mine for over 10 years now.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>pat jon kalsmith<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Jon, I'll tell him hi for you. He lives only a half mile from my shop.<P>At last report, he has over 30,000 miles on his Daily Driver V-8 Fiero.<P>I know that you were one of the VERY early members of NIFE, did you know that NIFE is celebrating it's 10th birthday this year?<P>Archie<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Dave Gunsul||06-27-2001||09:34 PM||||Montgomery Fest is on Aug. 12th<BR>I sent in a flyer about it but i'm not sure I made it for this months deadline for the<BR>newsletter. I havn't seen A Fiero yet in this show! <BR>There's also the Kendal County Dare car show<BR>in Yorkville but all the cars there, hotrods,<BR>muscle cars,new cars,etc are all in one class<BR>so it's almost impossible to win anything.<BR>I'm going to take my car in and just not register it. Date: Aug. 24th<BR>There's a ton of cruz-nighta around here too.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
